WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.626
Hi! There are lots of living things on our hands, but we can't see them. What are they? Today we'll learn about bacteria.

2
00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:16.314
Bacteria are very, very small. We need a microscope to see them.

3
00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:21.978
Bacteria are everywhere: in the air, in water, in soil, and on our bodies.

4
00:00:22.128 --> 00:00:28.602
Bacteria are living things. They grow and reproduce, and they reproduce very quickly.

5
00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:34.242
Some bacteria are useful to us, and some can make us ill.

6
00:00:34.392 --> 00:00:38.754
Useful bacteria help turn milk into yoghurt and cheese.

7
00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:44.586
Some bacteria, like fungi, help break down dead plants and animals.

8
00:00:44.736 --> 00:00:49.218
Harmful bacteria can make people ill and make food go bad.

9
00:00:49.368 --> 00:00:56.586
Washing hands with soap before eating and after using the toilet removes many bacteria.

10
00:00:56.736 --> 00:01:02.514
Watch out! Some pupils think all bacteria are bad. That's wrong!

11
00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:07.098
Some bacteria make yoghurt, and some break down dead things.

12
00:01:07.248 --> 00:01:13.482
It's the harmful ones we need to guard against, so wash your hands often.

13
00:01:13.632 --> 00:01:21.762
Your turn! What do we need to see bacteria? Pause and think.

14
00:01:21.912 --> 00:01:28.314
Bacteria are tiny, so we need a microscope. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:37.842
Another one! Which food is made with the help of useful bacteria? Pause and think.

16
00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:43.962
Yoghurt is made with useful bacteria. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:44.112 --> 00:01:52.914
Here's another! Why should we wash our hands before eating? Pause and think.

18
00:01:53.064 --> 00:02:00.618
To wash away harmful bacteria, so we're less likely to get ill. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:09.114
Try one more! Are bacteria living things? Pause and think.

20
00:02:09.264 --> 00:02:17.226
Yes. Bacteria grow and reproduce, so they're living things. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:17.376 --> 00:02:26.562
Try one more! Why does food go bad if it's left out too long? Pause and think.

22
00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:33.402
Bacteria and fungi grow on the food and spoil it. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:42.330
Last one! Can we see bacteria with just our eyes? Pause and think.

24
00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:51.114
No. Bacteria are too small. We need a microscope to see them. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:51.264 --> 00:03:02.058
Remember: bacteria are so small we need a microscope to see them. Some are useful and some are harmful. Washing your hands often helps protect you.

26
00:03:02.208 --> 00:03:07.290
Before your next meal, wash your hands well with soap!

